  "cloud-enablement-20261013" [label="Actual efficient\nmsc-math cloud work\nPARKED", shape=box, fillcolor="#f1f0ed", color="#93918c", tooltip="Source support/reference retained at2c88aaa5. Work and Claude clone/report ZIP route observed; Claude skipped required reading. Evidence at meta-topics/development-environment/cloud-surface-check-20261013. Broader outcome/efficiency unverified. Claude later supplied a received full-reading correction; counts matched pinned input, without validating whole-workflow success. Entry revision delivered: root AGENTS now 98 lines / 7131 bytes with rule preservation and surface-contract reviews; owner procedures routed explicitly. Coordination serving/source record repair passed checks and live HTTP. No automatic-loading, Rust/PDF or behavioral benefit established. Local source revision committed at f8242b43. Further five-minute Rust check approved, but native browser inventory is empty; ready-to-copy external relay retained, with no cloud run claimed. Stage timing and disproportionate finalization assessment retained with entry revision. At 19:09 UTC user requested no attachments and short Android copy/paste. Relay shortened to 389 characters with <=900-character text return; earlier ZIP requirement superseded. Applied batched preparation and compact Luna review. Human relay overhead corrected the recommendation: isolated compile probe put on hold; bundled Rust-readiness proposal prepared within five-minute analysis, with a new 15-minute cap pending approval. No live result. Jörn reported submission of the 15-minute readiness proposal at 19:21:32 UTC; result pending, cloud start not independently observed. Received user-relayed Claude report: Rust1.94.0/components auto-installed by rustup; workspacecheck0/55s, productionanchors4passed/148s,235s total, clean2c88 source. Independent source review found no contradiction; no rawcloudlogs. Current Rust runtime paths unchanged from tested input. Remaining Python/TeX/Sage/R2 plans delegated in parallel and retained as unexecuted candidates. Unsupported <10% estimate retracted. Requested handoff at meta-topics/development-environment/cloud-handoff-20261013/HANDOFF.md records correct target/authority/evidence and links user/assistant-only chat. Broader cloud objective not claimed complete. 14October audit: this resumed attempt failed to deliver the whole support workflow; two reply deadlines unambiguously missed. ExistingChrome connection observed, Claude state not verified. Two workers interrupted; whole task remains stopped. Earlier mutation used the wrong task ID and did not update this row; corrected by the postmortem.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Stopped by Jörn on13October22:53:56UTC and again23:05:39UTC. The earlier resumed support allowance was2h from22:33:19UTC, zero questions/novel permissions and10%weeklyquota. It is not current execution authority after the stop. Current authorization is postmortem only; no reset, publication, host/config changes or cloud execution.\nnext_step: Preserve dated evidence and this postmortem. No execution or permission request; resume only on an explicit new user instruction.\nSources: meta-topics/agent-workflow/cloud-session-failure-20261013.md, meta-topics/agent-workflow/cloud-continuation-prompt-20261013.txt, meta-topics/project-management/handoff.md, meta-topics/development-environment/cloud-surface-check-20261013/README.md, meta-topics/development-environment/cloud-entry-revision-proposal-20261013.txt, meta-topics/development-environment/cloud-entry-revision-20261013/README.md, meta-topics/agent-workflow/cloud-support-postmortem-20261014/README.md"];
