ng extra worktrees and specified build/download residue\nBounded research value and checked approach map\nOdd regular pair angular containment\nAsymmetric partner fixed-width plateau\nGeometric symmetric-partner exposition\nTest an unrestricted translation-cover optimization primitive\nVisual explanation of the circle-deficit method\nTen-minute preliminary check of local-cover continuum proof\nIndependent local-cover continuum and certificate-interface review\nFirst new affine tensor containment discriminator\nRepair evaluable research decision context after human feedback\nCompare compact exposition with and without the proved 5×7 example\nReconcile introduction and conclusion with selected symmetric-partner theorem\nFind the next exact contact obstruction for the 5×7 affine systolic maximum\nAssess a global arbitrary-partner cover obstruction or structural bound\nTest the next odd-pair full-tensor containment case\nCompare candidate journal-paper arcs and expose proof/readability gaps\nDisposition of existing file-viewer diff\nCurrent official-source administrative requirements\nExact product-capacity implementation contract\nShared agent controls consumed directly\nGeometry and local systolic frontier\nCombinatorial/duality frontier\nWider convex/symplectic connections\nCurrent mathematical frontier source audit\nRecent AI-assisted mathematics workflows\nMulticut convex-order variation\nGlobal product extremizers and external truncated-square conjecture\nIndependent polar embedding proof and transfer review\nOpen-ended mathematical value review\nSimplex and squared-body research figures\nIndependent simplex and LOP4 proof audit\nIndependent squared-body theorem audit\nSource audit of squared-body symmetry implication\nIndependent BMP Conjecture 6.1 counterexample audit\nIndependent full-orbit HKO mathematical audit\nIndependent HKO certificate replay\nRank-four zonoid Pfaffian inequality\nSix-dimensional simplex action-polar local witness\nOne coherent audited research paper\nFresh independent whole-paper mathematics review\nRoot all-page final PDF inspection\nSubstantially stronger HKO-descended body\nTriangle product position separation\nIndependent 20-facet HKO ascent audit\nIndependent all-dimensional difference-volume audit\nIndependent all-partner product theorem audit\nIndependent assembled paper reader/value/source review\nAudited 17-facet derivative and effective HKO witness\nTest two arbitrary characteristic-invariant hinges for 12-facet ascent\nIndependent moderate HKO mathematical coverage and volume audit\nFrozen fresh-copy moderate HKO replay\nSource ZIP, manifest, replay and verified link\nFinal research results have durable discovery routes", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#e7f1e8", color="#93918c", tooltip="Separate coordination, browser views and reusable knowledge\nCanonical coordination and browser source contract complete; five HTTP checks passed. Prior Chrome inspection unavailable.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md, meta-topics/project-management/thesis-work.md, meta-topics/project-management/handoff.md\n\nRoute process knowledge into project collaboration guidance\nLocal collaboration rules and knowledge routing complete; link/state checks passed. Behavioral and post-compaction performance untested. On 3 October, added Jörn-requested continuity guidance: brief acknowledgments do not stop unfinished authorized work; completion, explicit stopping and visible required-input boundaries remain. Rationale retained in commentary; behavioral effect untested.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected. Jörn subsequently requested the narrow acknowledgment/continuation correction in the Codex walkthrough on 3 October.\nSources: AGENTS.md, meta-topics/agent-workflow/collaboration-rationale.md, docs/knowledge/README.md\n\nSet up authorized workstation-only OpenObserve telemetry\nLive workstation logs/traces/metrics API-verified after daemon restart. Host implementation complete; maintenance belongs to ~/.dotfiles/INSTALL.md. Browser login unverified.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: meta-topics/development-environment/development-environments.md, meta-topics/development-environment/otel-design.md\n\nPrepare repository-owned skill migration\nReviewable local skill/discovery migration proposal returned; planner assignment ended. Candidate, activation and fresh-client acceptance remain unselected.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md\n\nPlan process-knowledge cleanup and behavioural evaluation\nReviewable two-link cleanup and bounded forward-pilot proposal returned; planner assignment ended. Cleanup and pilot remain unselected.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/knowledge-evaluation-plan.md\n\nSemantic msc-math project map dashboard\nSemantic DOM portfolio view completed in dedicated design session: whole msc-math goal, completion branches, interactive outcome/status/owner/blocker/scope/evidence/next-step nodes and shared prerequisite links. Live desktop/390px and320px fixture checked; no horizontal overflow.15second refresh preserves open state/focus. Root integrated source/dependency checks and8 HTTP tests.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md\n\nDefine support and handoff routes across selected environments\nRead-only supported-route matrix returned: local .agents source plus proposed Claude links/import; retained packets and manual host handoff initially. Independent-thread live delivery and SSH persistence remain unverified; Codex Cloud privileged-image/R2 bootstrap assumptions are not validated for Claude.\nplan_gap: Claude fresh-clone setup/discovery, cloud-to-host handoff, remote-device review access and reconnect/session continuity have no agreed acceptance route. Required support versus explicitly deferred capabilities is unresolved.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: meta-topics/development-environment/development-environments.md, docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md\n\nDefine truthful usage and spending observations\nRead-only recommendation returned: current.json and retained outcomes own durable PM state; OpenObserve is diagnostic. Optional explicit packet-event JSONL-to-OTel helper only if selected; no broker/database. Token/time observations are not billing; quota/USD unknown and independent-root/cloud usage is not covered.\nplan_gap: Comparable cloud/Pro usage, semantic task/message journaling and budget-enforcement mechanics are undefined. Numeric thresholds are not agreed; the selected delivery may explicitly defer automation.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: meta-topics/agent-workflow/collaboration-rationale.md, meta-topics/development-environment/development-environments.md\n\nWhole-project completion map and dependency projection\nWhole msc-math outcome/dependency map retained: workflow subproject, thesis support/prose and human PASS, code/evidence, reproduction, actual delivery/archive and closure. Twelve independent read-only candidates plus optional research/writing routes are visible without execution authorization. Semantic dashboard is primary; DOT/SVG source-hash projection checks pass.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md\n\nRetained implementation and artifact claims match their support\nCurrent candidate code/artifact claims received bounded source, count, path and API-contract review; two numerical defects repaired, all 52 literal local path occurrences resolve, retained exact evidence verified. Flow production correspondence remains explicitly bounded; this is not a whole-implementation proof.\nplan_gap: No need for blanket code cleanup or a universal solver formalization; inspect exactly what retained claims require.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-numerical.md, docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/acceptance-source-review.md\n\nClose surviving source repairs and reader-comment dispositions\nPrior seven source obligations remain dispositioned; continuation also supplies missing prediction methods and fixes rational/dyadic wording. No open blocking finding in the bounded independent patch review; human PASS and overall DS scope remain unknown.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nnext_step: Bounded run closed; preserved evidence and remaining project limits govern any later authorized continuation.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-restart-2026-10-04/ds-comment-disposition.md, docs/history/thesis-continuation-2026-10-04/acceptance-review.md\n\nAudit selected theorem and empirical wording against evidence\nAll 11 required areas mapped against selected sources, final PDF and evidence. Independent bounded reviews found no remaining blocking scoped finding; fixed-facet/equality/upper-section, empirical and conditional-flow limitations preserved. No unrestricted verification or human PASS implied.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nnext_step: Bounded run closed; preserved evidence and remaining project limits govern any later authorized continuation.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-continuation-2026-10-04/acceptance-review.md, docs/history/thesis-continuation-2026-10-04/acceptance-manifest.json\n\nAssemble and inspect one exact reader-facing candidate\nFinal101-page candidate d27e2f53… binds61thesis files at source00d03ceb… and independent acceptance81f5d804…. Complete page-level review/all11required-area map; prior100-page artifact preserved. The commit containing this state retains the delivery.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped. The oct04-candidate restart authorizes bounded thesis/repository improvement until 02:00 UTC; human PASS, public release and university submission are not implied.\nnext_step: Bounded run closed; preserved evidence and remaining project limits govern any later authorized continuation.\nSources: docs/history/thesis-continuation-2026-10-04/candidate-manifest.json, docs/history/thesis-continuation-2026-10-04/acceptance-manifest.json\n\nLoad checker and bounded watch outcome\nRead-only checker integrated and independently reviewed; 13 focused tests pass. Bounded observer interrupted after Jörn ended the discussion; full planned watch not established. Last retained 17:30:52Z snapshot had no errors/advisory signals; overload and semantic queue unknown. Observer role lacked