ary or superior; recommendations remain hypotheses. Completion covers the assigned returns only.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: Preliminary source mapping and discussion within the repair intake. No raw-rollout crawl, active incident migration, evaluations, substantial execution, configuration changes or further delegation.\nnext_step: Retain source-qualified return and compare concrete paths with Jörn; do not infer a selected incident architecture or evaluated remedy.\nSources: docs/history/coordination/20261003-project-repair-user-report.md, docs/knowledge/README.md, meta-topics/agent-workflow/collaboration-rationale.md, docs/coordination/intake-approach-options.md, docs/coordination/problem-knowledge-source-map.md\n\nCheck readable browser delivery of the goal map\nLuna corrected default SVG scaling after observing tiny labels. Isolated headless Chrome verified the served page, node selection and necessity filter. Wide graph requires horizontal scrolling. This establishes presentation behavior, not the model or intervention efficacy.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: Conceptual map retired after Jörn’s 10 October Q11 response; exact prior model/rendering is recoverable in Git. No current map maintenance is selected.\nSources: docs/history/retired-paths.json\n\nCompare mechanisms for making problem knowledge usable\nCandidate report compares decision-triggered retrieval, task-entry context delivery and change-driven reconciliation. Each includes probes and failure signs; no activation or efficacy established.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: Use the comparison to choose a concrete information-producing probe, checking past attempts and application failures.\nSources: docs/coordination/problem-knowledge-interventions.md\n\nTry existing knowledge routes for a communication problem\nFresh consumer recovered scoped cases and local positive interaction evidence, but no general effective remedy. Message-review skill records a negative live trial with an unlinked host-only antecedent. This is one observed retrieval pass, not a general inventory or causal diagnosis.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: Candidate next investigation: recover an exact disputed-answer/intervention case; do not repeat the failed skill as an established fix.\nSources: docs/coordination/problem-knowledge-probe.md\n\nDocument Codex implementation and make project overrides explicit\nRelease-matched Codex reference and source-only refresh helper complete at CLI/daemon 0.160.0. Project agent limits and selected flags are explicit; model/effort remain host-owned. Maintenance and explicit config-edit approval rules are documented. All 154 flags have generated registry descriptions, candidate consumer links, fresh values, project overrides, provenance and first-pass screening; historical runtime versions remain unknown. Two bounded source reviewers returned time/budget/cache and encryption findings, integrated by this coordinator with no worker obligation remaining. Source inspection establishes the legacy timeout no-op, model-selected V2 semantics and lack of a supported encryption-disable toggle; production plaintext-forcing patch efficacy is unverified. Jörn approved the automatic time-reminder setting as a provisional trial: 60-second system-clock reminders after user/tool output, with interruptible sleep available. Applied config comments record that he considers this cadence fast; usefulness and cache/cost effects are unmeasured. Jörn also explicitly approved the provisional context trial B: context metadata/tools and a 20,000-token pre-compaction warning, with the history/notes extension off. Developer-message retention, mailbox deferral and deferred-tool world state were not selected because no concrete solved problem was identified. Rollout budget remains off; its injected messages count remaining weighted tokens and it has no uncapped count-up-only mode or dedicated flag-registered query tool. Existing get_goal reports cumulative goal token/time usage with optional cap and automatic continuation; no goal or new meter was selected. Schema and fresh loader checks passed; inventory regenerated. Existing-thread adoption and runtime benefit remain unverified. No host config edit, build, restart or paid cache pilot. Runtime observation at22:14UTC: this running root received repeated timestamp developer messages and context-window metadata; get_context_remaining returned120014. Worker reconciled only docs/codex.md and docs/codex-config-proposals.md; root reviewed. Delivery in this root is observed; exact config provenance/cadence, threshold warning, other agents, continuity and benefit remain unverified.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn requested a repository documentation/source-navigation reference and explicit repo config overrides on 3 October; then explicitly excluded model/effort from repo overrides. Source checkout is for inspection only. No host config edit, CLI build/install, daemon restart or paid trial. Jörn subsequently explicitly approved enabling the proposed automatic time reminders, marked provisional/in test, in this thread; context-budget proposal B remains unapproved. Jörn explicitly approved enabling and provisionally marking token_budget; other considered flags were not selected. His cumulative expenditure preference authorizes source investigation/documentation, not creation of a goal, limit or meter.\nnext_step: Recheck source after CLI/model-catalog changes; select any orchestration trial separately. Host legacy timeout comment and historical rationale gaps remain documented, without silently editing another owner’s host config.\nSources: meta-topics/development-environment/codex-reference.md, .codex/config.toml, scripts/update-codex-source.sh, docs/codex-features.md, docs/codex-features.json, docs/codex-config-proposals.md, scripts/codex-feature-inventory.py\n\nAbsolute-path workstation file viewer\nProject viewer implemented and running behind Tailscale HTTPS /files. Absolute paths identify files across main/worktrees, artifacts and scratch directories. Markdown and config views work; dashboard links use their own checkout and retain dated source checks. Eight viewer and eight dedicated-dashboard tests pass; HTTPS bytes/data checks pass. Browser device/layout access unverified. Transient service requires starting again after machine reboot. Jörn accepted the explicit /absolute/path → HTTPS /files/absolute/path mapping as unambiguous; that exact line is now in AGENTS.md.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn explicitly selected creating the prototype as a proper project tool, with a one-line AGENTS.md path-to-URL rule; earlier session scope allowed repairing file serving. No broader workflow migration or thesis execution authorized.\nSources: docs/file-viewer.md, scripts/serve-files.py, scripts/test_serve_files.py, docs/dashboard/README.md\n\nBounded root scope supervision\nUser-requested bounded scope supervision completed: initial checkpoint review caught two stale hook decisions and premature parent closure; renewed supervisor independently read actual native visible actions and sent three count-up observations during useful audit/repair to root+worker. Receipt via root confirmed; older worker direct sibling acknowledgment failed. Final narrow assessment found original local passive-attribution/discovery/delivery obligations complete, with no user-only decision. Review points respected; no permanent/sustained-effectiveness or universal route guarantee.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Bounded work under Jörn’s request for supervision and correction of root derailment; no permanent mechanism, config activation, scientific run or paid API.\nnext_step: Assignment reviewed and released. Reuse supervision when useful in later selected work; observation responsibility does not end at conversation boundaries.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/current.json, meta-topics/project-management/handoff.md\n\nReconcile withdrawn usage-hook references\nWorker corrected only four stale C references in docs/codex.md, docs/coordination/README.md, scripts/README.md and scripts/subtree-usage.md. Root reviewed the withdrawal disposition. Historical candidate retained; no activation approval pending; counters/on-demand command remain and parent outcome is open. No code/config/guidance change.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Bounded work under Jörn’s request for supervision and correction of root derailment; no permanent mechanism, config activation, scientific run or paid API.\nnext_step: Assignment reviewed and released.\nSources: meta-topics/development-environment/codex-reference.md, docs/coordination/README.md, scripts/subtree-usage.md\n\nAudit native telemetry completion accounting\nReproduced and fixed raw SSE polling rows being treated as invalid usage completions and erasing known cache-write0. Raw observations now separate; malformed/partial/unmarked missing usage still diagnosed, raw-only tokens unknown.20 focused tests pass. Recent-root-only whitelist query observed omitted absent fields and29 valid parsed completions with no projection/regression errors. Raw-SSE branch source/fixture verified, not live exercised; native export dedup remains unverified and no live duplicate charging established.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Bounded diagnosis and same-worker repair continuing the selected local resource-attribution outcome; no config/service, n