trieve governing student record and chair/examiner-specific guidance before personal applicability/signability conclusions.\nSources: docs/history/official-requirements-check-20261023.md\n\nExact product-capacity implementation contract\nOne capacity_4d product route checked against selected manuscript, code and theorem. No mismatch established. Finite correspondence test source contains three fixtures; tests were not run and all-input correctness or other interfaces are not certified.\nproject: msc-math\nauthorization: Bounded source audit within assigned project; no proof research or numerical producer.\nnext_step: Use retained inspected scope to select the next unreviewed contract rather than repeating this check or claiming whole-code acceptance.\nSources: docs/history/code-contract-review-20261023.md\n\nShared agent controls consumed directly\nSix canonical shared workflows linked with project scope preserved. Actual msc fresh-consumer receipt and cross-repository source-repair task pass; no thesis source changed.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Jörn approved fleet active-source consolidation 28 October 2026, governing elapsed walltime and authorizing parallel work. No thesis work, publication, account or security changes.\nnext_step: No remaining msc-specific work in this package. Fleet owner retries global Claude body receipt at 13:30 Berlin; broader thesis/workflow acceptance remains separate.\nSources: AGENTS.md, .agents/skills/README.md, /workspaces/agent-fleet-tools/docs/intervention-work-goal.md, /workspaces/agent-fleet-tools/docs/consolidation-trial-results-2026-10-28.md\n\nGeometry and local systolic frontier\nExact fixed HKO t=3/10 body and portable complete-capacity/volume packet delivered: 20 facets, 75 simple vertices, ratio 1.0519141388294875... above HKO. Separate mathematical audit and fresh-copy replay passed; printed theorem in final r6.\nproject: research-20261028\nSources: topics/capacity-and-qp/convex-systolic-optimization/sections/hko-moderate.tex, topics/capacity-and-qp/convex-systolic-optimization/certificates/hko-t03/README.md\n\nCombinatorial/duality frontier\nSharp global six-dimensional simplex bound and unique equality class passed fresh math and exact polytope-coverage audits; portable four-script replay handed to paper worker. HK2019 primary thesis confirms four-dimensional 3/4 bound is known.\nproject: research-20261028\nSources: PLAN.md\n\nWider convex/symplectic connections\nAll-dimensional two-confocal-paraboloid strict difference-volume theorem and sharp limit passed fresh audit; six-page geometric section handed to paper worker. Planar squared-body factor five and checked CT transfer follow; no three-paraboloid claim.\nproject: research-20261028\nSources: PLAN.md\n\nCurrent mathematical frontier source audit\nHK2019 MSc thesis retrieved and its four-simplex Theorem B identified; bounded HKO-instability prior-art search found no earlier unrestricted ascent in inspected primary sources.\nproject: research-20261028\nSources: PLAN.md\n\nRecent AI-assisted mathematics workflows\nRecent primary-source workflow update retained in topics/literature/open-thesis/discovery.md; polar-product claim carefully labeled.\nproject: research-20261028\nSources: topics/literature/open-thesis/discovery.md\n\nMulticut convex-order variation\nWeighted seven-cut 17-facet ascent, effective all-ten-cut near-zero certificate and exact first-order obstruction for one or two characteristic-invariant affine hinges delivered and independently audited. Old rows retained; same- and distinct-facet cuts covered; no arbitrary twelve-facet local maximality.\nproject: research-20261028\nSources: topics/capacity-and-qp/convex-systolic-optimization/sections/hko-ascent.tex, topics/capacity-and-qp/convex-systolic-optimization/sections/hko-two-hinge-main.tex, topics/capacity-and-qp/convex-systolic-optimization/certificates/hko-two-hinge/README.md\n\nGlobal product extremizers and external truncated-square conjecture\nStrict Viterbo for every convex partner of a genuine corner-truncated parallelogram, uniform partner gap and Hausdorff-open factor neighborhood passed fresh audits; BMP proposed optimizer false, corrected classification open. Modules handed to paper worker.\nproject: research-20261028\nSources: PLAN.md\n\nIndependent polar embedding proof and transfer review\nTargeted external polar-product proof audit found no gap, no full Lean build. Unequal-strip lens and Toda-template volume obstructions show no HKO improvement by these transfers; branch parked.\nproject: research-20261028\nSources: PLAN.md\n\nOpen-ended mathematical value review\nCompared research lines and supplied squared-body tent proof, independently audited; recommended exploration beyond solved lines.\nproject: research-20261028\nSources: PLAN.md\n\nSimplex and squared-body research figures\nScratch Pfaffian graph and cap diagrams generated and visually inspected; diagrams do not prove the scalar inequality.\nproject: research-20261028\nauthorization: Selected by the active research coordinator within the 2026-10-29 10:05 UTC local research envelope; root owns integration, commits and cleanup.\nSources: PLAN.md\n\nIndependent simplex and LOP4 proof audit\nFour-dimensional 3/4 and equality proof mathematically audited; HK2019 primary thesis now establishes bound is prior art, so only proof/equality method may be new.\nproject: research-20261028\nauthorization: Selected by the active research coordinator within the 2026-10-29 10:05 UTC local research envelope; root owns integration, commits and cleanup.\nSources: PLAN.md\n\nIndependent squared-body theorem audit\nBoth planar factor-five theorem and stronger all-dimensional two-confocal-paraboloid theorem passed fresh mathematical audit; no result for three or more paraboloids.\nproject: research-20261028\nauthorization: Selected by the active research coordinator within the 2026-10-29 10:05 UTC local research envelope; root owns integration, commits and cleanup.\nSources: PLAN.md\n\nSource audit of squared-body symmetry implication\nConditional Chaidez–Tanny transfer to right-quaternionic-I invariant four-bodies checked against primary source; four-dimensional sharpness not established.\nproject: research-20261028\nauthorization: Selected by the active research coordinator within the 2026-10-29 10:05 UTC local research envelope; root owns integration, commits and cleanup.\nSources: PLAN.md\n\nIndependent BMP Conjecture 6.1 counterexample audit\nFresh global audit passes strict all-partner truncated-parallelogram theorem; separate neighborhood audit passes uniform gap and Hausdorff-open factor family. BMP optimizer counterfamily already audited.\nproject: research-20261028\nauthorization: Selected by the active research coordinator within the 2026-10-29 10:05 UTC local research envelope; root owns integration, commits and cleanup.\nSources: PLAN.md\n\nIndependent full-orbit HKO mathematical audit\nPassed full GL4 compressed proof, normalization, projection and equality; independent replay separately checked certificate.\nproject: research-20261028\nauthorization: Selected by active research coordinator within local research envelope ending 2026-10-29 10:05 UTC; root owns integration, commits and cleanup.\nSources: PLAN.md\n\nIndependent HKO certificate replay\nExact replay passed 18 rows, four identities, 62 facets, 360 feasible words and 80 transported identities; six altered controls rejected.\nproject: research-20261028\nauthorization: Selected by active research coordinator within local research envelope ending 2026-10-29 10:05 UTC; root owns integration, commits and cleanup.\nSources: PLAN.md\n\nRank-four zonoid Pfaffian inequality\nSeparate seven-page note retained and component-audited; bounded all-size mechanism attempt stopped at concrete blocker. Universal conjecture remains open; owner released.\nproject: research-20261028\nauthorization: Selected by active research coordinator within local research envelope ending