  "__parked" [label="UNSELECTED / PARKED · no execution\nCommunication diagnosis · BLOCKED\nSkill migration candidate · PARKED\nKnowledge cleanup / pilot · PARKED\nCloud automation · PARKED\nHistorical stop respected · DONE\nOptional result routes · PARKED\nOpen research packages · PARKED\nWriting method trial · PARKED\nDefine consequential friction and the stopping judgment · READY\nSpecify a comparison that can reject a candidate mechanism · READY\nCompare coordination at one integration boundary · READY\nSelect a version-aware per-thread prompt-composition view · READY\n3 Oct window selection · DROPPED\nLocal-maximality proofs and certificate navigation · DONE\nExact product-family proofs · DONE\nEmpirical interpretation and numerical example · DONE\nReproduction and evidence availability · DONE\nIndependent local-theorem review · DONE\nNumerical API-contract review · DONE\nCoupled instruction, knowledge and portability diagnosis · DONE\nResearch preparation approach comparison · DONE\nResearch agenda comparison · DONE\nIncomplete research preparation proposal · PARKED\nHistorical automatic context-reset cause audit · DONE\nChoose how the new uniform product method enters the writeup · PARKED\nResearch discoveries are accessible from main checkout · READY", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#f1f0ed", color="#93918c", tooltip="Determine why agent communication tools failed\nBounded local diagnosis finished. Same daemon persisted through failures; multiple TUI MCP server processes turned over. Stale endpoint binding is plausible, but old-port ownership, shutdown/rebind evidence and original cause are unavailable. Current list verifies reads only.\nblocker: Historical endpoint ownership/binding evidence is unavailable; current successful reads do not establish original cause or legacy send recovery.\nplan_gap: Capture failing URL, socket owner/PID and endpoint-binding lifecycle events on the next natural failure. Do not launch repeated investigation or restart the shared daemon.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/current.json\n\nOptional local skill candidate, activation and fresh-client tests\nProposed nine-skill local package, Claude discovery adapters and focused acceptance route. Keep outside loaded paths until selected. This is a candidate route, not an assignment.\nplan_gap: Initial instruction was inspect/plan/discuss first; migration and activation selection absent.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md\n\nOptional knowledge cleanup and forward pilot\nChoose retain-and-observe, two-link cleanup only, or cleanup plus bounded A/E pilot. No model calls or cleanup are launched by this plan.\nplan_gap: Scope, owner and resources have not been selected; broader cases and post-compaction validation remain unperformed.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/knowledge-evaluation-plan.md\n\nPossible cloud communication, setup and accounting automation\nExternal surfaces remain outside workstation telemetry. Live cloud messaging, detailed returned event logs and enforcement are possible mechanisms; required support and value are undecided.\nplan_gap: No agreed need, design, acceptance contract or authorization for cloud automation.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: meta-topics/development-environment/development-environments.md\n\nPrevious thesis stop superseded by 4 October authorization\nThe previous stop was respected until Jörn authorized this new bounded thesis/repository run. This historical task is closed; oct04-candidate owns current execution.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Historical stop respected until explicit restart; oct04-candidate owns current scope.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/handoff.md\n\nReview optional research/result selection\nHarmonic blind directions, ridge circulation, moment counterexample and joint-representation separations remain unselected. Symmetric-partner theorem moved to selected thesis scope on 3 October; presentation and proof acceptance remain open.\nplan_gap: Remaining optional results are unselected; the general zonotope bound remains conjectural/paused.\nproject: research\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a bounded statement/evidence/value comparison before any research execution or thesis addition.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md\n\nStructure a bounded future mathematical research packet\nThe dated scientific view records F=11/global HKO questions as outside the submission route; project facts distinguish non-generic arbitrary-polytope support from generic smooth-branch results. These are possible future questions, not current theorem obligations or assigned experiments.\nplan_gap: Exact question, owner evidence baseline, useful alternatives and resources have not been selected; recheck source owners before promoting historical open questions.\nproject: research\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a bounded problem-structuring packet; no large proof search, producer or Pro handoff follows automatically.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md, docs/dashboard/thesis.html\n\nConsider a discriminating authoring-workflow trial\nA current-source passage trial may inform authoring value, but local trials cannot certify whole-thesis readiness. Source repairs have independent value and do not depend on this optional mechanism.\nplan_gap: No trial candidate, success criterion, cost or human-review package selected; retrospective writing outcomes are not a general reliable method.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a concrete trial only if it could change the authoring route enough to justify its cost.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md\n\nDefine consequential friction and the stopping judgment\nOpen judgment about what costs matter for actual MSc project work, what constitutes repair success, and when further investment is worthwhile. No numeric target inferred from examples.\nplan_gap: No grounded baseline or agreed distinction between successful repair and justified stopping with unmet goals.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: Discuss concrete project consequences and alternative stopping interpretations; this does not block unrelated bounded intake.\nSources: docs/history/retired-paths.json, meta-topics/agent-workflow/collaboration-rationale.md\n\nSpecify a comparison that can reject a candidate mechanism\nCandidate bounded comparison on one source-grounded decision and later correction; fixture, receiving surface, observable outputs and integration owner not selected.\nplan_gap: Existing returns do not establish which discovery/application mechanism is worth deploying or whether an exact case is adequately reconstructable.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: Choose a concrete case and a discriminating result before investing in implementation; include prior negative evidence and opportunity costs.\nSources: docs/coordination/problem-knowledge-interventions.md, docs/coordination/problem-knowledge-probe.md\n\nCompare coordination at one integration boundary\nCandidate interface rehearsal comparing central, peer and bounded-integrator arrangements. No clean retrospective topology comparison or superiority claim available.\nplan_gap: How coordination changes parent-context demands, unresolved obligations and human rescue is not measured.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: If selected, compare handling of concurrent outputs, an unresolved integration obligation and a late correction; avoid three full project lifecycles.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md, meta-topics/agent-workflow/process-audit/REPORT.md, docs/history/retired-paths.json\n\nSelect a version-aware per-thread prompt-composition view\nAccepted handoff from 01a102da-b805-7f72-ae02-ba9842fa80a8; receipt saved at /tmp/msc-math/prompt-view-handoff-receipt.txt; sender receipt is not established. Bounded inspection found native CODEX_ROLLOUT_TRACE_ROOT request bundles in pinned source. Installed activation, complete deferred inventory, provenance and partial/delta reconstruction remain unverified. Design at ~/.codex/artifacts/recurring-data-2026-10-03/prompt-view-design.txt.\nplan_gap: Full runtime capture and freshness/coverage contracts not yet exercised.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Receiving inspection/design only. Implementation, environment/config activation, paid capture, build and restart remain unselected; config implications stay with sender.\nnext_step: Locate one existing native bundle or propose a narrowly approved future capture; verify schema and gaps before choosing a renderer.\nSources: meta-topics/development-environment/codex-reference.md\n\nSelect autonomous work while Jörn is available\nThe 3 October selection window expired without approval for substantial scientific execution. Its bounded preliminary calibration and source corrections remain at their scientific owners; the old time and budget request has no continuation authority.\nproject: research\nauthorization: 3 October user request selects prioritization, bounded preliminary planning and collection of necessary human decisions for an approximately six-hour capacity window. Substantial package selection and paid spending are not established.\nnext_step: Any later scientific programme requires a fresh selected scope and authorization. Preserve the completed preliminary sources; do not reactivate this dated window.\nSources: AGENTS.md, meta-topics/agent-workflow/collaboration-rationale.md, meta-topics/project-management/thesis-work.md, topics/empirical-studies/discovery-design/desk/research-agenda.md, docs/history/coordination/thesis-selection-2026-10-03/selection-structure.md, docs/history/coordination/thesis-selection-2026-10-03/execution-proposal.md, docs/history/coordination/thesis-selection-2026-10-03/alternative-comparison.md, docs/history/coordination/thesis-selection-2026-10-03/ready-decisions.md, meta-topics/project-management/expired-window-retention-2026-10-12.md\n\nLocal-maximality proofs and certificate navigation\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/07-hko.tex\n\nExact product-family proofs\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/09-rotated-regular-polygons.tex, thesis/chapters/10-affine-pentagons.tex, thesis/chapters/11-product-position.tex\n\nEmpirical interpretation and numerical example\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/08-data-science.tex, thesis/chapters/13-numerics.tex\n\nReproduction and evidence availability\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: thesis/chapters/14-code-data.tex, meta-topics/development-environment/installation-workflow.md\n\nIndependent local-theorem review\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Original task stopped; no running assignment.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: docs/history/coordination/thesis-execution-2026-10-04/restart-disposition.md\n\nNumerical API-contract review\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Original task stopped; no running assignment.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integration and acceptance records.\nSources: docs/history/coordination/thesis-execution-2026-10-04/restart-disposition.md\n\nCoupled instruction, knowledge and portability diagnosis\nBounded diagnosis retained; no repair or fresh-cloud acceptance implied.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Historical bounded10October work recovered from337f;12October cleanup authorizes retention/integration only, not activation or research execution.\nnext_step: Use retained findings if a later programme is selected; no old launch window or prompt is active.\nSources: meta-topics/agent-workflow/research-enablement-20261010/README.md\n\nResearch preparation approach comparison\nDated alternatives retained; no current programme selected.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Historical bounded10October work recovered from337f;12October cleanup authorizes retention/integration only, not activation or research execution.\nnext_step: Use retained findings if a later programme is selected; no old launch window or prompt is active.\nSources: meta-topics/agent-workflow/research-enablement-20261010/README.md\n\nResearch agenda comparison\nScientific comparisons retained; one-question-first sequencing recommendation withdrawn.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Historical bounded10October work recovered from337f;12October cleanup authorizes retention/integration only, not activation or research execution.\nnext_step: Use retained findings if a later programme is selected; no old launch window or prompt is active.\nSources: meta-topics/agent-workflow/research-enablement-20261010/README.md\n\nIncomplete research preparation proposal\nPreparation remains incomplete; premature ninety-minute launch request withdrawn, not pending approval. Named surfaces removed invented cloud-target/access blocker.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Historical bounded10October work recovered from337f;12October cleanup authorizes retention/integration only, not activation or research execution.\nnext_step: Use retained findings if a later programme is selected; no old launch window or prompt is active.\nSources: meta-topics/agent-workflow/research-enablement-20261010/README.md\n\nHistorical automatic context-reset cause audit\nSource-qualified10October runtime diagnosis retained with inactive patch. No present configuration or behavior acceptance.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Historical bounded10October work recovered from337f;12October cleanup authorizes retention/integration only, not activation or research execution.\nnext_step: Use retained findings if a later programme is selected; no old launch window or prompt is active.\nSources: meta-topics/agent-workflow/research-enablement-20261010/README.md\n\nChoose how the new uniform product method enters the writeup\nConcrete reader decision: keep the short accepted pentagon proof as main anchor plus general theorem/method and appendix estimates, or make the uniform proof central. No automatic new theorem promotion.\nproject: research-20261019\nnext_step: After the concrete calibration reader check, consider the uniform-method manuscript route. A broader question draft was not sent; no automatic theorem/appendix promotion.\nSources: topics/products/pentagon-affine-products/odd-regular-angular-width.md, thesis/chapters/09-rotated-regular-polygons.tex, thesis/chapters/10b-symmetric-partners.tex\n\nResearch discoveries are accessible from main checkout\nMain38c0488e lacks the two completed research commits and this discovery repair. Main has unrelated dirty viewer files and an untracked live-task graph that must survive integration.\nproject: research-20261028\nnext_step: Fleet root selects a concrete local adoption route, preserves main edits and verifies main discovery; current repair explicitly does not merge main.\nSources: PLAN.md, STATUS.md"];
  "__candidates_thesis" [label="THESIS · READY IF SELECTED\nFoundations / QP\nVariation / certificate\nProduct proof bridges\nDS reader disposition\nFigures / numerical example\nAI reflection map", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Check current foundations and QP exposition\nRead Chapters 2 and 4 against backlog items 1: terminology, Rudolf input/output, cyclic-word operation and dependence/vertex-replacement bridges. Return surviving/solved/withdrawn findings with exact source locations; no edits or theorem strengthening.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded read-only Chapter 2/4 packet in its own worktree.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/thesis-work.md\n\nCheck variation and HKO certificate navigation\nRead Chapters 6/7 and HKO appendix against backlog item 2; separate finite predicates and geometric implication. The certificate and slope-to-neighborhood proof are reported present. No certificate recomputation.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded source-navigation review; coordinate Chapter 7 edits with the claim packet.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/thesis-work.md\n\nCheck product-family finite and limiting proof bridges\nRead Chapters 9–11 against backlog item 3: ordered pairings, finite vertex/alternation calculations, equality classification, product-position squeeze and Hausdorff/capacity-continuity bridge. Preserve exact/numerical distinctions.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select an independent product-proof source packet; report exact surviving bridges before edits.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/thesis-work.md\n\nDispose of reader concerns against the selected DS chapter\nMap retained human comments to current Chapter 8/appendix: applied, absent, context-accepted or older-draft-only. Preserve accepted correlation/area text, retrospective bounds and explicitly unresolved random_F8_s3_45. Human acceptance and overall DS scope remain separate.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a source-aware DS disposition packet; do not import old rejection as a current verdict.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/thesis-work.md\n\nCheck visualization purposes and certified numerical example\nInspect Chapters 12–14 for panel purpose/inference limits and the requested concrete certified numerical example; return a scoped proposal using existing code/evidence without launching producers.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a read-only example/provenance design packet before implementing or running it.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/thesis-work.md\n\nVerify AI annotation repairs against the selected source\nCheck selected Chapter 15 against the mapped v3 repairs; no confirmed annotation defect remains. Preserve factual disclosure separately from reflection and record source drift or unknown whole-chapter acceptance.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded source-map check; do not rewrite unflagged AI prose.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/thesis-work.md"];
  "__candidates_evidence" [label="EVIDENCE · READY IF SELECTED\nChapter 7 claim check\nCode correspondence\nArtifact traceability", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Check rendered Chapter 7 claims and PDF/source identity\nIdentify source revision/PDF identity, then compare L10-N/L10-N+ rendered statement, equality family and upper-section-curvature caveat against 24 September disposition and non-HKO rational/analytic packet. If no matching PDF is available, report that prerequisite; do not treat the older frozen PDF as current.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select the bounded rendered-PDF claim audit; no expensive verifier rerun.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/thesis-work.md, docs/consolidation/2026-09-24/claim-disposition.md, topics/variation-and-local-maxima/hko-local-maximum/non-hko/README.md, topics/variation-and-local-maxima/hko-local-maximum/non-hko/PROOF.md\n\nCheck retained algorithm and numerical contract boundaries\nTrace retained capacity/numerics/flow promises to crate APIs and focused evidence owners; distinguish theorem assumptions, bounded tests and optimized production correspondence. Return exact claim/contract gaps and recommended focused checks; no blanket implementation rewrite.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select read-only claim/API/evidence mapping in a separate worktree; test execution requires its chosen packet.\nSources: crates/README.md, docs/project-facts.md, meta-topics/repository-organization/README.md\n\nResolve displayed examples, counts and public artifact references\nMap named KKT/comparison/product counts, figures and annotated HKO listing to canonical packets and actual tracked/registered/public availability. Existing local files do not establish a public commit or remote download promise.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded current-claim-to-artifact inventory; preserve producer-owned outputs.\nSources: meta-topics/project-management/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
  "__candidates_reproduction" [label="REPRODUCTION · READY IF SELECTED\nReproduction inventory", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Compare the reproduction playbook with retained thesis promises\nSelected13figure producer/input/publication-copy/PDF routes now mapped and executed, with versions, comparisons and explicit limits. Remaining opportunity concerns full historical producer, LICCA hardware/timing and long-horizon reproduction coverage.\nplan_gap: Independent candidate route; no separate assignment under this ID. Selected restart coverage is recorded under oct04-candidate and its owned packets.\nproject: reproduction\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Keep remaining full-producer/long-horizon scope separate from completed selected-figure route.\nSources: docs/figure-reproduction.md, docs/reproducibility.md"];
